---
source: https://www.daringgourmet.com/how-to-make-golden-syrup/
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 1 hour
total time: 1 hour 5 minutes
servings: 24
---

Place @cane sugar{4%cups} and @water{1.25%cups} in a #saucepan{} and stir to combine. Bring it to a boil, stirring regularly to prevent burning until the sugar is dissolved. Stir very gently to prevent sugar water from splashing up the sides of the saucepan.

Once boiling, gently stir in @lemon juice{2%Tbsp} (either fresh or bottled will work, though fresh produces a better flavor) or @citric acid{1/2%tsp}.

Reduce the heat to a very low and gentle simmer and leave the saucepan uncovered. Do not stir the syrup again. Let it simmer on very low for 40 to ~{60%minutes} or longer until the sugar turns a rich amber color (about 240°F to 250°F on a #candy thermometer{}).

Turn off the heat and let it sit for a few minutes, then pour the hot syrup into a #jar{} and let it cool completely before closing with a tight-sealing lid. Store at room temperature for several months.

Tip: This makes approximately 3 cups of golden syrup. If your syrup cools too thick and stiff, reheat it gently while adding a splash of water. If your syrup is too runny, simmer it longer to caramelize further.
